  "verified": false,
  "note": "HAND-MAINTAINED. Two kinds only: mpc (금통위) and fomc — about eight meetings a year each, published a year ahead, and between them what actually moves the KRW curve. CPI prints and bond auctions are deliberately excluded: they would push this past fifty entries a year and turn it into a maintenance job for a fraction of the value. Korea's MPC held twelve rate meetings a year through 2016 and eight from 2017; unscheduled meetings are included where they matter — the 2020-03-16 emergency cut above all. \"verified\": false means THESE DATES ARE A SEED, reconstructed by the assistant from the published-schedule pattern rather than copied from an authoritative source. A weekday cross-check flagged ~23 of them as landing off the usual Thursday (MPC) / Wednesday (FOMC), so a real share of them are simply wrong. Check against bok.or.kr and federalreserve.gov, correct what is wrong, then set verified to true. guards/calendar.test.ts fails when the last entry is under 60 days away — that failure is the reminder to top the file up.",
